Phase 3-5 of bd-e3069d: plan a contiguous ready prefix, submit merge-async with exact selected head, persist and poll UUID state, distinguish merged/enqueued/failed/indeterminate, prove lower-head race semantics in a disposable repository, and opt in only after all-or-none provider evidence.

## Disposable-provider acceptance result (2026-07-31)

The full evidence is recorded in `docs/validation/github-native-stack-sandbox-2026-07-31.md`.

Proven: selected-top stale SHA rejection with zero merges; lower fast-forward after 202 failed all eight entries with zero merges; full and partial-prefix direct squash success; exact remaining-entry retarget/rebase; UUID pending polling; terminal success/failure; exact HTTP 409 recovery of the same UUID; and sealed indeterminate handling after response loss.

Critical negative result: after 202, lower PR #23 was rewound from `7c26d64d...` to its base `c46c03b...`, preserving upper ancestry. GitHub returned `merged` for UUID `322d1e78-a2f0-43be-aa09-2fb56e803ce8` and marked all three selected PRs merged at the changed lower generation. The API leases only the selected top SHA. Cara can detect this post hoc but cannot prevent it.

Therefore this slice may land planner/checkpoint/poll/receipt primitives, but `github_stack_backend_read_only` must remain closed. Phase-5 executable opt-in is rejected until GitHub supplies a complete-group generation lease or an equivalent preventive mechanism.

## Implementation (`43018b2`, candidate Cara 0.0.68)

Added `src/github/stack_merge.rs` with:

- exact maximal contiguous ready-prefix selection over complete generation-bound scheduler evidence;
- direct-squash-only submit plans carrying every ordered lower PR/head plus the selected top SHA;
- one final full Stack generation read immediately before the single PUT;
- sealed, self-contained UUID checkpoints and one-step bounded polling for scheduler-owned cadence/deadlines;
- typed submitted/pending/enqueued/merged/failed/indeterminate receipts;
- exact HTTP 409 UUID adoption only when returned expected top SHA, method, and action match the sealed request;
- no retry after response loss without a UUID;
- terminal fresh default, selected PR, remaining PR, and Stack reads;
- `merged` proof only when all selected PRs merged at their exact sealed heads, provider result SHA matches default when supplied, and the open Stack suffix exactly matches the original unselected suffix;
- explicit indeterminate evidence for partial landing, lower-head generation drift, malformed/expired polling, or rediscovery failure;
- no `gh stack`, local tracking, sync, rebase, or link command.

The Stack topology reader now accepts GitHub's observed post-prefix shape: retained closed prefix followed by a rebased/retargeted open suffix beginning at the exact Stack base. It still rejects non-linear live open generations.

27 focused Stack tests pass; warning-denied all-target Clippy passes; all 755 tests pass serially under the pinned Nix shell. The normal parallel `just validate` currently exposes an unrelated v0.0.67 App-git child fixture environment race (711 pass, one failure twice; exact fixture passes); the owning agent was sent the reproduction for a baseline patch before reintegration.

